    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "I think first and foremost, we should keep in mind what James Madison said. We know what he talked about, the dangers of factionalism. But at the end of his writings, he said, the circulation of confidence, of trust is more important than the circulation of money. And his explanation was, if we ever lose trust in public institutions or with each other, then we're lost.",
