    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89077.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, a lesson to take away from this one, Andrew, is Tom Cruise flew an F-14 in the first one. And the second one is aboard a joint strike fighter. But you know, unlike what we do in America when we close down a coal mine and we go to producing solar power panels, the middle class, the enlisted of that aircraft carrier, we didn't throw them out. and say, you don't know how to work on this, we trained them for the next step. And so when I watched it, what was really missing in that movie, and all I could think about was the 5,000 sales on an aircraft carrier. Their average age, Andrew, 19 and a half. Oh my gosh. And so that's what I think about. I know Tom Cruise gets all the glory and well he should, but as General Akramayov, when he came on over here, he was chief of the Soviet Union General Staff. And Admiral Crowell took him everywhere. Admiral Crowell took him in a barbecue in Arkansas. He took him to military bases. His last stop was aboard an aircraft carrier. And when they had left it and come back, he said, well, Admiral Crowell asked a general contractor, what do you most get out of your entire time in America? What did you most appreciate? And he said, you're enlisted men. Now",
