    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "Well, thank you so much, Joe. We do have to rekindle that sense of trust and belonging and community and millions of Americans and certainly having a 20 year old stand in front of the plane saying, look, I haven't hooked this and if I haven't, then. We're both going to die. There's nothing more inspiring than that, because you've placed your life in the hands of someone. And people in service have had to do that over and over again for years. It is that kind of spirit that the country needs, and I'm so grateful to you for believing in forward as a way to hopefully accomplish that. Do you think that, and this is something that I've actually gone somewhat deep on, do you think that some kind of mandatory national service might help instill a sense of community or belonging or trust? Because you've probably seen some of the proposals in that direction.",
