    "turn_text": "I'm sure people listening to you right now are thinking to themselves, holy cow, like this guy would make a great president, which by the way, I do think you'd make a great president. You and I spent some time together on the trail in 2020, and I was blown away by how You didn't seem to get a fair shake. And there's been something of a pattern, honestly, where I feel like, for whatever reason, the Democrats don't seem to know what they have in you or had in you in terms of the US Senate race in Pennsylvania. I think you should have been a US Senator. And then I think you should have been the president, honestly. That's the way I See it. And when you and I were on the trail together, you walked across the state of New Hampshire, kind of, again, reflecting a bit of a pattern for you, which is just trying to meet people and put yourself in their shoes and come across as a human being, which is kind of the opposite of the approach to politics that most people have. It's just you working hard to meet people where they are. And I thought that, I mean, I was, you know, in New Hampshire, not the same way you were when you walked across the state. How long did that take, by the way? That was a lot",
