    "turn_idx": 55,
    "turn_text": "Yes. She's a warrior. there's no one like or ever meant. And it did come back. And so everything's off the table. And we just worked it through. And the doctor said after six, eight months, whatever, I think we've got it back in remission again. I'd gotten in that first base in Congress, as I told you, as a payback tour to my country. Because we were in a hospital room. after they first said they couldn't get it at a military hospital. And she had four to maybe six or so months, but they couldn't get it out at the rest section. And it was glioblastoma. We went to children's hospital because my healthcare plan permitted me in the military to do that. And they saved her life for quite a period of time until it came back the second time. And I had to pay back my country. That's why I ran healthcare. This time, I thought we were okay. And again, then I got into the presidential race. But as you probably know, you do know is simultaneously as it was time to say it's unfair to ask people to continue to support me. It was also just then when the cancer had reoccurred a third time. So, and all, but it's the greatest thing in life was to have her.",
