    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89077.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 61,
    "turn_text": "We even had a memo from one of the lead, you know, the CNN, MSNBC, of Fox, and from one of them, we had a friend on the station sent me a copy of the memo saying not to have Joseph stack on. And the other one had a good friend, but he just said it ain't gonna happen. But you know, I think, I kinda learned that complaining about the media for a politician is like a sea captain complaining about the sea. And you just gotta accept it. I do think that it's a challenge at times, yes for me, but it also has, I think at times, you know, hurt the nation a little bit. In other circumstances, as the former head, I think it was of CBS said, you know, Mr. Trump is great for our ratings, you know, and how could they miss who and what he was going to bring or even the win the first time? But if you were out there on the deck plates, not just in a studio, I can remember after They put over about just about $10 million that Democratic Party did via unions, even though my union voting record was like 100%. And also direct from the Democratic Central Campaign Committee for my opponent, because we were like 24 points up with three, four weeks to go. And then all the money came in on an ad that the Washington Post gave for Pinocchio's to as being false and called a sleazy way to win. I couldn't complain it was over and OK, but I It's like they didn't, I was out there after that was over and went back as I did the first time to everyone in the 67 counties to say thank you. I also, because of Philadelphia congressional boss and Pittsburgh, college boss, wouldn't let me go to any of their democratic events. So I went to like 200 African-American churches and went back to slink them individually too. But the first county I went back to, it's Grant and County. They came together, you know, and I thanked them for their support. And I remember this woman stood up who was Vice Chair at something at the time and said, I just want you to know that I have relatives of mine who have voted Democrat this entire life period of theirs, but they're going to go for Trump. And I knew she was talking about her. And right then I said, no, if I'm getting this down in the death place, it means And somebody better be alert where this is not just a joke happening. But again, I stepped back to what you also said. He was a symptom of a problem. And I do believe that problem was, why couldn't we earn their trust? And when you're doing things from Washington DC, even the media, and constantly lobbying artillery shells, as I said, of these coal traditions back and forth, and never listening, very rarely saying there's a dialogue Because you think you'll get primary doubt, you're not willing to, you're willing for the expedient to lose your principle. I think that that is what has been most damaging and caused it.",
